<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Markus Sittikus von Hohenems</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1574">1574</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Markus Sittikus von Hohenems was prince-archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> from 1612 to 1619. He continued the rebuilding of Salzburg in Italian style begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolf-dietrich-von-raitenau">Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau</a>, starting the new cathedral designed by Santino Solari and building the palace and trick fountains of Hellbrunn.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/markus-sittikus-von-hohenems.jpg" alt="Markus Sittikus von Hohenems" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Boys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anthony_Bays_Hohenemser_Festtafel_1578_Markus_Sittikus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
